<LegalPage lang="en" title="Cookie policy" description="Cookie policy of Taller de Digitalización.">
  <section>
    <h2>1. What are cookies?</h2>
    <p>Cookies are small files that are downloaded to the user's device when accessing certain web pages.</p>
    <p>Cookies make it possible, among other things, for a website to work properly, remember certain preferences, obtain statistical information about browsing or make integration with third-party services easier.</p>
    <p>Similar technologies may also be used, such as pixels, tags, browser local storage, identifiers or third-party scripts. In this policy, the term “cookies” is used broadly to include these technologies where applicable.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>2. Controller</h2>
    <p>The party responsible for the use of cookies on this website is:</p>
    <p>
      Controller: Pablo Leone<br />
      Tax ID (NIF): 41675399C<br />
      Address: Numancia 4, Fuensalida, Spain<br />
      Contact email: info@tallerdedigitalizacion.com<br />
      Website: tallerdedigitalizacion.com
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>3. What types of cookies does this website use?</h2>
    <p>This website may use first-party and third-party cookies for different purposes.</p>
    <h3>3.1. Technical or necessary cookies</h3>
    <p>These are the cookies needed for the website to work properly and to provide the services requested by the user.</p>
    <p>They may be used, for example, to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>allow browsing the website</li>
      <li>remember technical preferences</li>
      <li>keep the site secure</li>
      <li>manage forms</li>
      <li>remember basic settings</li>
      <li>allow interactive elements to work</li>
    </ul>
    <p>These cookies do not require consent when they are strictly necessary to provide a service requested by the user or for the basic operation of the site.</p>

    <h3>3.2. Analytics or measurement cookies</h3>
    <p>These are cookies that provide information about how users use the website, which pages they visit, how long they stay, where they come from or what actions they take.</p>
    <p>This website may use Google Analytics 4 to analyse the use of the website and to improve its content, navigation, performance and calls to action.</p>
    <p>The information collected may include technical data such as IP address, browser, device, pages visited, interaction events, date, time and source of the visit.</p>
    <p>Google tags (Google Analytics 4 and Google Ads measurement) are loaded on every visit, but with consent <strong>denied by default</strong> (Consent Mode v2). Until the user accepts the corresponding category, no Google cookie is written and Google only receives technical signals without cookies, such as the page visited, the source of the visit (for example, campaign parameters) and browser data, in addition to the IP address of any connection. Those signals are not linked to a persistent browser identifier and are used to measure in aggregate and to estimate conversions. If the user accepts analytics, Google Analytics starts using cookies; if the user accepts marketing, Google Ads does too.</p>

    <h3>3.3. Marketing or advertising cookies</h3>
    <p>These are cookies that make it possible to measure the results of the ads that Taller de Digitalización publishes on Google{hasPixel ? ", Facebook and Instagram" : ""} and to attribute to each ad the enquiries it generates{hasPixel ? ", and to show ads to people who have already visited the website" : ""}.</p>
    <p>For Google ads, conversion measurement may store the ad click identifier in the <code>_gcl_aw</code> cookie. That cookie is only written if the user accepts the "Marketing" category in the cookie panel.</p>
    {hasPixel && (
      <>
        <p>This website may use the Meta Pixel, a service of Meta Platforms Ireland Limited. The pixel records page visits and actions such as booking a call, writing on WhatsApp, calling, sending an email or completing a form, and links them to the browser through the <code>_fbp</code> and <code>_fbc</code> cookies.</p>
        <p>The Meta Pixel is only loaded if the user accepts the "Marketing" category in the cookie panel.</p>
      </>
    )}

    <h3>3.4. Third-party cookies</h3>
    <p>This website may integrate or link to third-party services that may install cookies or similar technologies when the user interacts with them.</p>
    <p>These services may include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Google Analytics and Google Ads, for web analytics and ad measurement.</li>
      <li>Cal.com, for call bookings.</li>
      <li>Chatbase, for the chatbot or automated assistant.</li>
      {hasPixel && <li>Meta Pixel (Facebook and Instagram), to measure ads.</li>}
      <li>WhatsApp, to make direct contact easier.</li>
      <li>Technical services linked to custom forms or the site's own backend.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Each of these services may use its own cookies and process data under its own policies.</p>
  </section>

