  <section>
    <h2>5. Google Analytics and Google Ads</h2>
    <p>This website may use Google Analytics 4, a web analytics service provided by Google.</p>
    <p>Google tags are loaded with consent denied by default and are updated according to the user's choice in the cookie panel. Without consent, Google only receives technical signals without cookies, as described in section 3.2.</p>
    <p>Google Analytics makes it possible to analyse in aggregate how users browse the website, what content they read and what actions they take, in order to improve the site and measure its performance.</p>
    <p>Google may process data on servers located outside the European Economic Area. Google's processing of data is governed by its own terms and policies.</p>
    <p>The user can find more information in Google's privacy policy.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>6. Cal.com</h2>
    <p>This website links to Cal.com to allow free 30-minute calls to be booked. On most pages, Cal.com is not loaded inside this website: its page only opens when the user presses a booking button. On the landing pages for the software development and automation services, the Cal.com calendar is shown inside the page itself: it only loads when the user accepts cookies or presses the "See available times" button.</p>
    <p>When the user uses Cal.com, the user may enter data such as name, email, company, availability, comments or other information needed to manage the meeting.</p>
    <p>Cal.com may use its own and third-party cookies to provide its service, remember preferences, manage sessions or analyse the use of its platform.</p>
    <p>The use of Cal.com is also governed by its own terms and privacy policy.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>7. Chatbase</h2>
    <p>This website uses Chatbase as a chatbot or automated assistant.</p>
    <p>Chatbase may use cookies or similar technologies to make the chatbot work, keep conversations, analyse interactions or improve the service.</p>
    <p>The chat is only loaded if the user accepts the "Help chat" category in the cookie panel.</p>
    <p>The user should avoid entering sensitive or confidential information, credentials, business secrets, third-party data or unnecessary information into the chatbot.</p>
    <p>The use of Chatbase is also governed by its own terms and privacy policy.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>8. WhatsApp</h2>
    <p>This website includes links and a button to WhatsApp.</p>
    <p>By clicking them, the user leaves the website and accesses external services, which may use their own cookies or similar technologies.</p>
    <p>The owner of this website does not control the cookies installed by those third parties or their data processing policies.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>9. Consent</h2>
    <p>Necessary technical cookies may be used without prior consent, as they are needed for the basic operation of the website.</p>
    <p>Analytics, advertising or third-party cookies that are not strictly necessary generally require the user's prior consent under the applicable regulations.</p>
    <p>On the first visit, the website shows a banner that lets you <strong>reject</strong>, <strong>configure</strong> by category (analytics, help chat and marketing) or <strong>accept all</strong> non-necessary cookies. Rejecting is as easy as accepting.</p>
    <p>Google Analytics cookies, Google Ads cookies, {hasPixel ? "Meta cookies, " : ""}and Chatbase are not activated until the user gives consent for the corresponding category. Google tags are always loaded, with consent denied by default, and without consent they only send technical signals without cookies (section 3.2). The choice is kept for 12 months; after that, you are asked again.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>10. How to configure or disable cookies in your browser</h2>
    <p>The user can allow, block or delete the cookies installed on their device through the settings of the browser they use.</p>
    <p>Below are help links for the most common browsers:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Google Chrome: the browser's privacy and security settings.</li>
      <li>Mozilla Firefox: privacy and security options.</li>
      <li>Safari: privacy preferences.</li>
      <li>Microsoft Edge: cookie and site permission settings.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Blocking certain cookies may affect how some features of the website or of integrated external services work.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>11. Withdrawing consent</h2>
    <p>The user can change or withdraw consent at any time from the <a href="#" data-cookie-settings-open>Cookie settings</a> link, also available in the footer of every page, or by changing the browser settings. When analytics consent is withdrawn, the Google Analytics cookies of this domain are deleted, and when marketing consent is withdrawn, the Google Ads cookies{hasPixel ? " and the Meta cookies" : ""} are deleted.</p>
    <p>Withdrawing consent does not affect the lawfulness of processing carried out before.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>12. International transfers</h2>
    <p>Using third-party services such as Google Analytics, Google Ads, Cal.com, Chatbase{hasPixel ? ", Meta" : ""} or WhatsApp may involve international data transfers or processing carried out outside the European Economic Area.</p>
    <p>That processing will be governed by the safeguards, conditions and privacy policies that apply at each provider.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>13. Updates to this policy</h2>
    <p>This Cookie Policy may be modified when there are changes in the cookie configuration, the services used, the applicable regulations or the criteria of the competent authorities.</p>
    <p>Users are advised to review this policy periodically.</p>
    <p>Last updated: November 2026.</p>
    <p>This is a translation of the Spanish version. If there is any discrepancy, the Spanish version prevails.</p>
  </section>
